  "result": "Default list made once at `def` time, shared across calls. `append` mutates that same object, so `add(1)` leaves `[1]` in it, and `add(2)` appends to it \u2192 `[1, 2]`.\n\nFix: use `None` sentinel, build new list per call:\n\n```python\ndef add(x, items=None):\n    if items is None:\n        items = []\n    items.append(x)\n    return items\n```\n\nNow `add(1)` \u2192 `[1]`, `add(2)` \u2192 `[2]`.",
